venance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-determiners"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Check **several + distant**.","Distant plural things take **those**.","Choose **Those**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"This is singular and near.","B":"That is distant but singular.","C":"These is plural but near.","D":"Distant plural things take **those**."}}},{"id":"5301c0d2-745c-5f41-a655-ec22ec5b26d5","topicSlug":"demonstratives","level":"A1","prompt":"Point to one cup in your hand: “____ cup is mine.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Those"},{"id":"B","text":"This"},{"id":"C","text":"That"},{"id":"D","text":"These"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Check two features: **one** item and **near** the speaker.","explanation":"One nearby item takes **this**.","keywords":["near-singular"],"skill":"near-singular","contextKey":"demonstratives-50","fingerprint":"05ad2237b43fc9705ebd0dfa93caf5d3b599e127f3ad1228b714b6a42affab9b","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-determiners"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Check two features: **one** item and **near** the speaker.","One nearby item takes **this**.","Choose **This**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Those is both plural and distant.","B":"One nearby item takes **this**.","C":"That points away from the speaker; the item is explicitly in your hand.","D":"These is plural."}}},{"id":"2a85d645-b5a6-57a6-a314-537171b94281","topicSlug":"demonstratives","level":"A1","prompt":"Point to one cup far away across the room: “____ cup is yours.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"That"},{"id":"B","text":"This"},{"id":"C","text":"These"},{"id":"D","text":"Those"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"Check **one + distant**.","explanation":"One distant item takes **that**.","keywords":["far-singular"],"skill":"far-singular","contextKey":"demonstratives-50","fingerprint":"4dd681a397bdf5659987dd9e77a5efe4bb1f3343098b06df89956c4688c48a9a","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-determiners"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Check **one + distant**.","One distant item takes **that**.","Choose **That**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"One distant item takes **that**.","B":"This points to something near; the task explicitly places it far away.","C":"These is plural and near.","D":"Those is plural, but the task says one."}}},{"id":"41d0a2ea-0d2a-548f-ab7f-36d23c824564","topicSlug":"demonstratives","level":"A1","prompt":"Point to several cups beside you: “____ cups are ours.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"This"},{"id":"B","text":"That"},{"id":"C","text":"Those"},{"id":"D","text":"These"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Check **several + nearby**.","explanation":"Nearby plural things take **these**.","keywords":["near-plural"],"skill":"near-plural","contextKey":"demonstratives-50","fingerprint":"e0bac7111514e1e47094b39e47e72ff517a8006d472f491ccbe4a19d407c9ae0","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-determiners"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Check **several + nearby**.","Nearby plural things take **these**.","Choose **These**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"This is singular.","B":"That is singular and distant.","C":"Those is plural but distant; these things are beside you.","D":"Nearby plural things take **these**."}}},{"id":"1ab63f6b-a73b-5c18-afc9-a7e84c01042a","topicSlug":"demonstratives","level":"A1","prompt":"Point to several cups far away beyond the fence: “____ cups are theirs.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"This"},{"id":"B","text":"That"},{"id":"C","text":"These"},{"id":"D","text":"Those"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Check **several + distant**.","explanation":"Distant plural things take **those**.","keywords":["far-plural"],"skill":"far-plural","contextKey":"demonstratives-50","fingerprint":"0b8fa2fada5c1e3fbbd5f37495a4cb945ebcb275ad63648bf68d946d0d180ca4","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-determiners"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Check **several + distant**.","Distant plural things take **those**.","Choose **Those**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"This is singular and near.","B":"That is distant but singular.","C":"These is plural but near.","D":"Distant plural things take **those**."}}}],"chapter":{"introduction":["Choose words that point to things and distinguish number from distance.","The form tells you how to build the sentence; the context tells you why that form is useful. Read each section with both questions in mind. The examples make one contrast at a time, while the practice mixes the skills so that you learn to recognise the pattern yourself."],"rules":[{"title":"Near and far","explanation":"Use **this** for one nearby thing and **that** for one more distant thing. Distance can be physical or part of how the speaker views a situation. Demonstratives can stand alone or come before a noun.","pattern":"**This** seat is free. / **That** seat by the door is taken.","commonMistakes":["This and that are singular, even when the object seems large or contains many parts."],"examples":["Point to one book in your hand: “**This** book is mine.”","Point to one box in your hand: “**This** box is mine.”"],"skill":"form"},{"title":"Plural demonstratives","explanation":"Use **these** for nearby plural things and **those** for more distant plural things. Match the following noun and verb to plural number. Near and far are described explicitly in the practice so that the intended choice is clear.","pattern":"**These books are** mine. / **Those books are** yours.","commonMistakes":["These is pronounced differently from this. In writing, remember the final -e in these."],"examples":["Point to one book far away across the room: “**That** book is yours.”","Point to one box far away across the room: “**That** box is yours.”"],"skill":"meaning"},{"title":"Pointing without a following noun","explanation":"A demonstrative can function as a pronoun when the thing is already understood. It still has number: This is mine; These are mine. Do not add an unnecessary noun merely because the demonstrative has no following noun.","pattern":"What is **that**? / Who owns **these**?","commonMistakes":["The word it refers back to an identified thing but does not make the same near/far contrast."],"examples":["Point to several books beside you: “**These** books are ours.”","Point to several boxes beside you: “**These** boxes are ours.”"],"skill":"contrast"},{"title":"Referring to ideas and time","explanation":"This and that can refer to an event or whole idea. This week identifies the current week; that week points to a week already identified elsewhere. In conversation, that often responds to something just said.","pattern":"The train was cancelled. **That** was frustrating.","commonMistakes":["Real conversational choices depend on viewpoint. The questions here use explicit physical distance rather than judging subjective emphasis."],"examples":["Point to several books far away beyond the fence: “**Those** books are theirs.”","Point to several boxes far away beyond the fence: “**Those** boxes are theirs.”"],"skill":"application"}],"recap":["**This** seat is free. / **That** seat by the door is taken.","**These books are** mine. / **Those books are** yours.","What is **that**? / Who owns **these**?","The train was cancelled. **That** was frustrating."]},"stage":"1 · Sentence foundations","prerequisites":["present-simple-be"]}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT(version,slug) DO NOTHING;
